A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus compares the kingdom of heaven to a householder who hired labourers into his vineyard at the morning, the third, sixth, ninth and eleventh hours. At evening each received a penny, beginning from the last, and the first murmured. The householder answered with the agreement, his right to do what he will with his own, and a question about an eye that is evil. Jesus says before the parable, “But many that are first shall be last; and the last shall be first,” and after it, “So the last shall be first, and the first last: for many be called, but few chosen.” He gives no explanation and names none of the parts. The comparison says that the householder seeks labourers all day, keeps his word, does what he will with his own, is good, and reverses the order of first and last.'))
